"Eric" <eric@cook.rm-this-word.met.edu> writes:
> I suppose you're implying the ide driver for Alpha is not the same as for
> x86 linux and therefore doesn't necessarily support LBD48.

The support for LBA48 is chipset dependant: some older chipsets can while
some can't, same with the new chipsets. Then, you have the driver: if the
driver doesn't know anything about LBA48 (which is needed for drive larger
than 1xx GB) obviously it won't work.

> Is that correct? 

I haven't look at the ide code so I can't confirm.

> If so, I wonder why Jason Garrell's previous post stated, "I have the
> maxtor (rebranded promise card) and it is working fine in my AS 200 4/233
> with 4x160G disks". One assumes he's using linux and is therefore using
