> I know it does work for x86, but it seems that does not do the same in 
> Alpha.

'make install' for x86 really runs a script which does that:

# User may have a custom install script

if [ -x ~/bin/installkernel ]; then exec ~/bin/installkernel "$@"; fi
if [ -x /sbin/installkernel ]; then exec /sbin/installkernel "$@"; fi

followed by some further actions but 'exec' above means that if
such script will be found then all remaining stuff is "forgotten".

Nothing really stops you from doing the same even if some pieces
are currently missing.  I do not have Alpha handy in this moment
but, IIRC, at least on _some_ distributions /sbin/installkernel script
was actually present.  Keep in mind that "installing" kernel on x86,
in a presence of lilo or grub, is something else then a similar
action on Alpha and there will be further differences depending on
a boot loader you happen to use.

'mkinitrd' script is definitely presend in RH72 for Alpha.

  Michal


