Is the DECSERVER setup for telnet listener service?  If so, then you would
just telnet to the IP and port that you want to access the console on, just
like you access the terminal sever itself.  If the IP of the terminal server
was 90.0.0.1,  and you wanted to get to the console on port1, then you would
telnet to 90.0.0.1/port=2001 or something like that dependant on your IP
configuration, and your telnet program/service.  The telnet session defaults
to port 23 that is console for the terminal server itself.

Here is a log of setting up a whole server for telnet listener service for
use with consoleworks.  You will probably just need to verify and/or modify
the first 4 ports that  your console ports are plugged into.  You do not
need modify the entire server like I did.

I hope this helps you.

Mike Naime


