> kernel stack not valid halt
> PC = fffffc0000313144
> boot failure        

This usually happens when aboot switches to the kernel and something
goes wrong.  Try stripping the kernel to a bare minimum, leave only
network and nfs built in and compile everything else as modules.  Also
try turning off "Legacy start address" in the "Kernel hacking" section
during configuration.  Those things have helped me with the very same
problem.

