164LX motherboards use typical ATX power supplies.  And they are often
radically overclockable with, say, a 20+ CFM 60mm fan on the stock Alpha
heatsink.  They are also quite inexpensive now on eBay, but try to get one
that has at least been 'tested' (beware of duds).

My EV56 533MHz CPUs ran at 600MHz and never burped.  Supposedly, 667MHz 
was also attainable with the 533, but I never found the jumper 
configuration to go to 10x bus speed.  Hint:  the very inexpensive 
ThermalTake Volcano 5 Athlon cooler ($7, Fry's) has a great replacement 
fan bolted to it.  Just attach the beefier fan to the stock Alpha 
heatsink with some longer bolts.

Be advised that the LX's use PC100 EDO ECC DIMMs in Pairs.  Not as bad 
as, say, RIMM modules, but still a bit more costly than PC100/133 SDRAM.  
It was some time ago, but I think 256mb (2x128) set me back about $40 
or $45  shipped from a Pricewatch seller.

The ideal thing is to get your logic board with a CPU and at least some
RAM to get started.  

Good luck!

