Recently I installed RedHat7.2_alpha on my Compaq XP1000. During last
few weeks, there were 2 repeating problems related to my X window
display.

1. I often launch 'lock screen' instead of 'logout' when I am
temporarily away from my desk. Screen saver will start running when
the screen is locked. However, about every two weeks or so, the screen
saver would freeze on monitor display, and not respond to any keyboard
input. Remotely logining on to my machine will find the application
'X' is taking nearly 90% of the cpu time. Simply killing 'X' does not
free the frozen display either. The only solution has been shutdown
and reboot.

2. The second problem occurs more often, about every 4 to 5 days. In
this case, when I drag any window in my desktop with mouse to another
location, the window will not recover its original appearance. Part of
the window will lose its original content and color, which are
replaced by the color of desktop behind. After several move, the
appearance of the window will be totally lost in the color of desktop.
The window does recover its original appearance after I switch to
another session of desktop and then back to the initial session where
the window locates. There are several ways of rescue. Sometimes
switching to the linux console and back to X will solve the problem.
Logining out and in again seems also working. Sometimes I have to
reboot. Occasionally I have to shutdown and reboot. The most annoying
part is that none of these rescues fixes the problem permanently. It
will come back again within another week.

The desktop environment I use is KDE. The graphic card is ELSA Gloria
Synergy Controller with 8MB SGRAM and 3DLab's Permedia2 graphic chip.
Is there anyone who has similar problem before and/or has some clue?
Any feedback is appreciated.

