Mathieu Chouquet-Stringer <mathieu@newview.com> wrote:
> The only file it
> seems to recognize is a file called fwupdate.exe
> The problem: I don't know what it does

fwupdate.exe is the "first stage" firmware loader which will
load ROM image _when it will find one_.  In other words on your
floppy you need also at least a file with rom data to load; possibly
also a short text file which lists file name(s) to use.  I do not
remember details but there should some READMEs somewhere.

> with it because I've got no output

A likely assumption is that if you are using such "rescue" measures then
there is really no place to output anything because things are really
FUBAR; or your current firmware does not provide something which is
expected.  Quite possibly there is also no space to stick into an
emergency loader anything but a bare minimum.

  Michal


