> Is there an SRM variable I may set to get my Alpha to reboot automagically
> after a power failure? Right now, it powers off and stays off. Thanks in
> advance.

'auto_action' (BOOT) if I remember name correctly.  Try 'show auto*'
to check.  You need also set correctly 'bootdef_dev' and 'boot_osflags'.
The later the best idea to '0' with 'aboot.conf' giving a full default
boot command at label 0.  If you will make 'boot_osflags' to 'i'
then you will get as a result an "interactive aboot" which is a very
good idea for testing.

Everything may depend on how your power supply is rigged.

  Michal


